cudamatmul
==========

Square matrix product on the graphics card, written against CUDA 2.3.

Two kernels: the obvious one, where every thread reads its whole row and
column straight out of global memory, and a tiled one that stages 16 x 16
blocks in shared memory so each value is read once and used sixteen
times. Same result, several times faster.

Needs the toolkit and a card of compute capability 1.1 or better:

    make && ./cudamatmul_test

Without a card the host tests still run and the gpu ones are skipped.
There is also

    make emu

which builds the kernels for the cpu with -deviceemu. Do not try it on
anything much bigger than 128 x 128.
